# Keep the build context small and hermetic.
#
# node_modules is the big one: without this, `docker build` uploads the whole
# host install — including pnpm's symlink farm, which does not survive the
# transfer and produces dependency trees that differ from a clean install.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output. Copying a host .next into the image is how you ship a bundle
# built against the wrong platform.
**/dist
**/.next
**/.test-out
**/*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.gitignore
backups
docs
*.md

# Secrets must never enter an image layer. .env is read by compose on the HOST
# and injected as environment; it has no business in the build context.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
